prompt.text:
Implement a new TypeScript module exporting these declarations:

```typescript
export interface PanelSpec {
  key: string;
  title: string;
}

export interface FeatureManifest {
  imports: string[];
  providers: string[];
  routes: Array<{
    path: string;
    panelKey: string;
    metadata: { heading: string };
  }>;
}

export function buildFeatureManifest(
  panel: PanelSpec,
  services: readonly string[]
): FeatureManifest;
```

`panel.key` and `panel.title` must be strings containing at least one non-whitespace character. Each service must satisfy the same rule, and service names must be unique after trimming. Throw `TypeError` for malformed text and `Error` for duplicates. Trim valid values in the output without changing the inputs. The manifest must always contain imports in this order: `foundation`, `commands`, `validation`, `widgets`. Providers must preserve the service input order. It must contain exactly one route with an empty path, the trimmed panel key, and metadata heading equal to the trimmed panel title. Return entirely new arrays and objects with no aliases to the inputs. Empty services are valid.

Return only the complete source file; do not include Markdown fences or prose.

